{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgu3K2iUDhK4CztGHWHTb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0134FCQjiFaBG4wX8vkXWdLy","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-3334883877/worktree/.pose/adr/2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md","offset":230},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1300,"cache_read_input_tokens":72665,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1300},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"2e262851-9b9a-4cff-8069-8929f59c7a2d","timestamp":"2026-11-10T09:51:06.387Z","request_id":"req_011Cgu3K2V4z9rVs4FpoHMsP","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_0134FCQjiFaBG4wX8vkXWdLy":{"file_path":"/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-3334883877/worktree/.pose/adr/2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md","offset":230}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0134FCQjiFaBG4wX8vkXWdLy","type":"tool_result","content":"230\t  clients; an MCP transport gains no Execution Identity, signature or human presence\n231\t  of the CLI by calling the same function.\n232\t\n233\t## Related specs\n234\t\n235\t- [B31](../specs/2026-10-14-pose-common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff.md)\n236\t- [B33](../specs/2026-10-14-pose-bounded-isolated-graph-caches.md)\n237\t- [B35](../specs/2026-10-14-pose-optional-worktree-runtime.md)\n238\t\n239\t## Amendment: transport, identity and slicing of the worktree runtime (B35)\n240\t\n241\tDecided 2026-11-09 with the maintainer, before the functional start of B35:\n242\t\n243\t- **Transport.** A stream socket in the user's own directory: a Unix domain socket\n244\t  (Linux, macOS), mode 0600 in a 0700 directory owned by the user, whose peer is\n245\t  checked by the operating system's credentials (`SO_PEERCRED`, `LOCAL_PEERCRED`)\n246\t  before any byte is read. No TCP, no token, no network surface. Windows has no\n247\t  named-pipe implementation in this repository (the standard library has none and\n248\t  the repository takes no dependency for it): the runtime reports itself\n249\t  unsupported there and every command runs standalone. That is a declared\n250\t  limitation, not a silent one, and a named pipe with the owner's ACL is the\n251\t  follow-up that lifts it.\n252\t- **Identity.** user (uid) + canonical worktree (symlinks resolved) + Git common\n253\t  directory + engine version/build + wire protocol + schema. The endpoint name is\n254\t  a digest of the location part only (user, worktree, Git common directory), so two\n255\t  worktrees or two users never share an endpoint; the engine part is compared at the\n256\t  handshake, field by field, and a difference is refused naming it, so that a new CLI\n257\t  that finds an old process after an update is refused by name instead of being\n258\t  given a different endpoint and never learning the old one is there.\n259\t- **Authority.** The runtime of slice 1 hosts no domain operation: it answers\n260\t  handshake, status and stop. It confers no authority, signature or presence, and a\n261\t  client that attaches gains nothing it did not have standalone.\n262\t- **Slicing.** B35 is delivered in three specs, each reviewed on its own:\n263\t  `pose-optional-worktree-runtime` (identity, endpoint, handshake, lifecycle,\n264\t  standalone fallback: R1-R4), `pose-worktree-runtime-resident-cache` (R5, R7: the\n265\t  resident reuse of the B33 views, reconciliation, typed results) and\n266\t  `pose-worktree-runtime-qos-and-measurement` (R6, R8: budgets, short queries\n267\t  protected from heavy checks, measured thresholds). Budgets and thresholds are\n268\t  fixed from a measured synthetic corpus with a declared environment, never from a\n269\t  historical sample.\n270\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"09862aec-60ea-420f-9275-357e2b27513d","timestamp":"2026-11-10T09:51:06.393Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-3334883877/worktree/.pose/adr/2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md","content":"  clients; an MCP transport gains no Execution Identity, signature or human presence\n  of the CLI by calling the same function.\n\n## Related specs\n\n- [B31](../specs/2026-10-14-pose-common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff.md)\n- [B33](../specs/2026-10-14-pose-bounded-isolated-graph-caches.md)\n- [B35](../specs/2026-10-14-pose-optional-worktree-runtime.md)\n\n## Amendment: transport, identity and slicing of the worktree runtime (B35)\n\nDecided 2026-11-09 with the maintainer, before the functional start of B35:\n\n- **Transport.** A stream socket in the user's own directory: a Unix domain socket\n  (Linux, macOS), mode 0600 in a 0700 directory owned by the user, whose peer is\n  checked by the operating system's credentials (`SO_PEERCRED`, `LOCAL_PEERCRED`)\n  before any byte is read. No TCP, no token, no network surface. Windows has no\n  named-pipe implementation in this repository (the standard library has none and\n  the repository takes no dependency for it): the runtime reports itself\n  unsupported there and every command runs standalone. That is a declared\n  limitation, not a silent one, and a named pipe with the owner's ACL is the\n  follow-up that lifts it.\n- **Identity.** user (uid) + canonical worktree (symlinks resolved) + Git common\n  directory + engine version/build + wire protocol + schema. The endpoint name is\n  a digest of the location part only (user, worktree, Git common directory), so two\n  worktrees or two users never share an endpoint; the engine part is compared at the\n  handshake, field by field, and a difference is refused naming it, so that a new CLI\n  that finds an old process after an update is refused by name instead of being\n  given a different endpoint and never learning the old one is there.\n- **Authority.** The runtime of slice 1 hosts no domain operation: it answers\n  handshake, status and stop. It confers no authority, signature or presence, and a\n  client that attaches gains nothing it did not have standalone.\n- **Slicing.** B35 is delivered in three specs, each reviewed on its own:\n  `pose-optional-worktree-runtime` (identity, endpoint, handshake, lifecycle,\n  standalone fallback: R1-R4), `pose-worktree-runtime-resident-cache` (R5, R7: the\n  resident reuse of the B33 views, reconciliation, typed results) and\n  `pose-worktree-runtime-qos-and-measurement` (R6, R8: budgets, short queries\n  protected from heavy checks, measured thresholds). Budgets and thresholds are\n  fixed from a measured synthetic corpus with a declared environment, never from a\n  historical sample.\n","numLines":41,"startLine":230,"totalLines":270}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0134FCQjiFaBG4wX8vkXWdLy","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
