{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgu3K9aD735mPNzHPtsuE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011gJz1b8tkL4juQHocei5sW","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-3334883877/worktree/.pose/adr/2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md","offset":50,"limit":50},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1159,"cache_read_input_tokens":73965,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1159},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"c5ef8555-5fe6-4b69-8d49-0f934b43fcd8","timestamp":"2026-11-10T09:51:13.149Z","request_id":"req_011Cgu3K9JqUL4zkyvJNaYpK","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_011gJz1b8tkL4juQHocei5sW":{"file_path":"/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-3334883877/worktree/.pose/adr/2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md","offset":50,"limit":50}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011gJz1b8tkL4juQHocei5sW","type":"tool_result","content":"50\t- Preserve the scoped Git batch-reader decision. Residence does not authorize\n51\t  a shared cat-file stream, persistent/global reader pool or shell expansion.\n52\t  Any future change of its ownership/lifetime needs a separate structural decision.\n53\t- Make runtime optional, identified by user + canonical worktree/Git identity +\n54\t  engine/build/protocol/schema/capabilities. project_id/common Git directory alone\n55\t  cannot distinguish mutable worktrees. A separate protected local IPC endpoint\n56\t  may host this domain; platform transport (Unix socket/named pipe or equivalent),\n57\t  authentication/permissions and compatibility require resolution before code.\n58\t  Never take a client's MCP stdio connection or claim a static doctor sees it.\n59\t- Support explicit attach/start/status/stop/restart and standalone/CI fallback.\n60\t  Restart/update must not inherit stale generation/authority. An ambiguous committed\n61\t  write requires receipt/reconcile before retry through another process; query\n62\t  fallback validates inputs. Watch events are hints; B14/B15/B34 own publication,\n63\t  coordination and coherent read generations, including external edits.\n64\t- Bound requested evaluation concurrency by category/worktree and globally, with\n65\t  CPU quota/affinity, memory/IO/child-process and admission metrics. Protect short\n66\t  queries during heavy work and preserve deterministic output. Fix budgets and\n67\t  benchmark thresholds on comparable corpora before adoption, rather than changing\n68\t  defaults from one historical sample or claiming p95 from three observations.\n69\t\n70\t## Consequences\n71\t\n72\tB31 yields standalone semantic reuse, B33 supplies isolated/bounded graph views,\n73\tand B35 consumes both after B07/B12/B14/B15/B32/B34 prerequisites. API/caches can\n74\tbe qualified without requiring a resident service; B35 stays opt-in after delivery.\n75\tThe exact IPC/protocol, compatible GateResult/envelopes, platform support, cache\n76\taccounting/view ownership and lifecycle/QoS thresholds remain acceptance work.\n77\tNo new root enumeration, command, default, workflow queue or policy is adopted.\n78\tHistorical benchmark numbers and the duration of documentary checks do not prove\n79\truntime speedup. Consumers retain existing mutable contracts until qualified\n80\tmigration, and the source/effects/assurance remain authoritative.\n81\t\n82\t## Alternatives rejected\n83\t\n84\t- Mirror all .pose into RAM at startup: loads cold history and retains repeated\n85\t  parsing/copying/algorithms without establishing freshness or a memory budget.\n86\t- Reuse the MCP client's stdio as shared IPC: the stream belongs to its initiating\n87\t  client and supplies neither attach compatibility nor authority for another CLI.\n88\t- Fork CLI rules in MCP/runtime: improves transport at the cost of divergent\n89\t  result, validation and authorization semantics.\n90\t- Treat watcher events or mtime/clean as proof: misses external changes and cannot\n91\t  bind a gate/write to complete current inputs.\n92\t- Run arbitrary validation checks in a new in-process MCP helper: bypasses the\n93\t  established execution-identity/approval/Harness boundary.\n94\t- Mandatory autostart and unlimited work/cache: removes CI/standalone fallback,\n95\t  risks memory growth and query starvation without a measured benefit.\n96\t\n97\t## Review triggers\n98\t\n99\tBefore B31/B33/B35 start, settle interface/compatibility, caller mapping, local IPC"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"9d8ae6f9-8aaa-4ea0-9b4d-c7cdf7cb506c","timestamp":"2026-11-10T09:51:13.154Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-3334883877/worktree/.pose/adr/2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md","content":"- Preserve the scoped Git batch-reader decision. Residence does not authorize\n  a shared cat-file stream, persistent/global reader pool or shell expansion.\n  Any future change of its ownership/lifetime needs a separate structural decision.\n- Make runtime optional, identified by user + canonical worktree/Git identity +\n  engine/build/protocol/schema/capabilities. project_id/common Git directory alone\n  cannot distinguish mutable worktrees. A separate protected local IPC endpoint\n  may host this domain; platform transport (Unix socket/named pipe or equivalent),\n  authentication/permissions and compatibility require resolution before code.\n  Never take a client's MCP stdio connection or claim a static doctor sees it.\n- Support explicit attach/start/status/stop/restart and standalone/CI fallback.\n  Restart/update must not inherit stale generation/authority. An ambiguous committed\n  write requires receipt/reconcile before retry through another process; query\n  fallback validates inputs. Watch events are hints; B14/B15/B34 own publication,\n  coordination and coherent read generations, including external edits.\n- Bound requested evaluation concurrency by category/worktree and globally, with\n  CPU quota/affinity, memory/IO/child-process and admission metrics. Protect short\n  queries during heavy work and preserve deterministic output. Fix budgets and\n  benchmark thresholds on comparable corpora before adoption, rather than changing\n  defaults from one historical sample or claiming p95 from three observations.\n\n## Consequences\n\nB31 yields standalone semantic reuse, B33 supplies isolated/bounded graph views,\nand B35 consumes both after B07/B12/B14/B15/B32/B34 prerequisites. API/caches can\nbe qualified without requiring a resident service; B35 stays opt-in after delivery.\nThe exact IPC/protocol, compatible GateResult/envelopes, platform support, cache\naccounting/view ownership and lifecycle/QoS thresholds remain acceptance work.\nNo new root enumeration, command, default, workflow queue or policy is adopted.\nHistorical benchmark numbers and the duration of documentary checks do not prove\nruntime speedup. Consumers retain existing mutable contracts until qualified\nmigration, and the source/effects/assurance remain authoritative.\n\n## Alternatives rejected\n\n- Mirror all .pose into RAM at startup: loads cold history and retains repeated\n  parsing/copying/algorithms without establishing freshness or a memory budget.\n- Reuse the MCP client's stdio as shared IPC: the stream belongs to its initiating\n  client and supplies neither attach compatibility nor authority for another CLI.\n- Fork CLI rules in MCP/runtime: improves transport at the cost of divergent\n  result, validation and authorization semantics.\n- Treat watcher events or mtime/clean as proof: misses external changes and cannot\n  bind a gate/write to complete current inputs.\n- Run arbitrary validation checks in a new in-process MCP helper: bypasses the\n  established execution-identity/approval/Harness boundary.\n- Mandatory autostart and unlimited work/cache: removes CI/standalone fallback,\n  risks memory growth and query starvation without a measured benefit.\n\n## Review triggers\n\nBefore B31/B33/B35 start, settle interface/compatibility, caller mapping, local IPC","numLines":50,"startLine":50,"totalLines":270}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_011gJz1b8tkL4juQHocei5sW","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
